      "notes": [
        "Hi-Fi Suture, Ultra High Molecular Weight Polyethylene, is a braided, nonabsorbable suture indicated for soft tissue repair in orthopedic procedures. The high performance fiber used to create the braided suture is extremely strong and provides exceptional strength for knot tying. The unique construction of the suture creates low-profile knots. In addition, the inherent material characteristics of the suture provide ease of use for suture passing and tying."
